WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.780
Symbolic links are normal filesystem features.

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:10.200
They are useful for compatibility, organization, deployment layouts, and operational workflows.

3
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:17.580
The security issue appears when software treats a path string as if it permanently identifies the object the developer had in mind.

4
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.700
A path is input.

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:28.280
It may come from a user, a configuration file, an environment variable, a service working directory, a package layout, or another component.

6
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:34.780
The path may contain link components, relative parts, or names in directories that other actors can modify.

7
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:42.480
The program should not assume that the string alone proves the final object is safe to read, write, replace, or delete.

8
00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:48.680
Symbolic-link handling affects confidentiality when a program reads from or writes to a different object than intended.

9
00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.580
It affects integrity when content is modified through an unexpected path.

10
00:00:53.680 --> 00:01:00.080
It affects reliability when cleanup removes the wrong file or when replacement logic publishes incomplete state.

11
00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:05.380
These concerns are engineering problems around trust, identity, and lifetime.

12
00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:10.220
Safe handling begins by separating path strings from file objects.

13
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.640
A path can be resolved later and may be influenced by directory state.

14
00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:22.420
An opened descriptor or handle is a concrete object reference that the program can validate and operate on according to the platform's rules.

15
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:36.300
This course focuses on defensive design: trusted directories, race-aware workflows, descriptor-first operations, safe creation and replacement, permissions, cleanup, traversal policy, testing, and review.

16
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.440
The goal is maintainable file handling that does not depend on hidden path assumptions.
